Short instructions:

1. Download the files password_manager.py and password_manager_gui.py and move them to your HOME directory.
2. Download the file password-manager.desktop and place it on the desktop.
3. For all files, open Properties and enable “Allow executing file as program” (make them executable).
4. Install Python, Tkinter and cryptography (how to do this is described in the text below).
5. Launch the program from the desktop icon.
6. To change the master password, use the terminal program: password_manager.py.

Regarding the master password:
1. Choose a password of 6 or 7 or 8 words that have no connection whatsoever to your past, present, or future life.
2. Separate the words with digits that also have nothing to do with your past, present, or future life.
3. Write the password down on a piece of paper and, at first, enter it 3 to 5 times so that the body’s muscle memory is activated. 
4. After one week, destroy the password written on paper.
5. Enter the password every day so you do not forget it. Do not skip a single day.
Keep entering the password every day for as long as you use this program.
